    "text": "<p>A conducting ring of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;and resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is placed in a region of uniform time varying&nbsp;magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;which is perpendicular to the plane of the ring. If the magnetic field is changing at a rate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi></math>, then the current induced in the ring is</p>\r",
